The '''Mygeeto Campaign''', also known as the '''assault on Mygeeto''', or '''campaign on Mygeeto''', was a three-[[Standard year|year]] campaign of the [[Clone Wars]] between the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]. It consisted of several battles, including the [[Third Battle of Mygeeto]] and the [[Fourth Battle of Mygeeto]], the latter of which took place during the [[Outer Rim Sieges]]. [[Jedi General]] [[Ki-Adi-Mundi]] and the [[Galactic Marines|21st Nova Corps]] were deployed to [[Mygeeto]] to capture it from the Separatists during the campaign. However, during the campaign, Mundi was [[Death|executed]] by his [[clone trooper]]s under [[Order 66]].

==The battle==
{{Quote|Come on, we must take the bridge!|Ki-Adi-Mundi to his clones|<ref name="Galaxy's Edge 2" />}}
The campaign to take [[Mygeeto]] was fought for three [[standard year]]s.<ref name="Force Collection1">{{ForceCollection|Bacara|star=4}}</ref> During the [[Third Battle of Mygeeto]], [[Jedi General]] [[Depa Billaba]] and her [[Depa Billaba's second battalion|battalion]] fought against [[General]] [[Grievous]] and his forces. While Grievous managed to escape, the Republic was victorious and [[Colonel]] [[Coburn Sear]] was [[Death|killed]].<ref name="First Blood 5" /> However, mere [[Standard month|months]] later, a [[Fourth Battle of Mygeeto]] began.<ref name="Helmet Collection 15" /> During this battle, [[Jedi]] General [[Ki-Adi-Mundi]] led the [[Galactic Marines|21st Nova Corps]] against the [[Separatist Droid Army]]. However, during the battle, [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]] issued [[Order 66]], which compelled all of the [[Grand Army of the Republic]]'s [[clone trooper]]s to turn on and [[Death|execute]] their Jedi commanding officers<ref name="ROTS" /> via secret [[Behavioral modification biochip|control chips]] implanted in their [[brain]]s.<ref name="Orders">{{TCW|Orders (episode)}}</ref> Mundi attempted to rally his [[trooper]]s on a bridge spanning a chasm between two [[city]] blocks, with enemy [[droid]]s destroying several [[tank]]s, but his troops had been given their new directive.<ref name="ROTS" />

The troopers complied, and moments later the clones near Mundi stopped charging. Confused, Mundi turned around and was blasted by his troopers' fire. The surprised [[Jedi Master]] managed to [[Death|kill]] three Marines by deflecting their fire before succumbing to his troops' shots.<ref name="ROTS" /> Prior to Order 66, [[Jedi]] [[General]] [[Jaro Tapal]]'s [[13th Battalion]] was ordered to reinforce Master Mundi’s forces on Mygeeto, but the Chancellor's order ultimately meant they never arrived, as the battalion was killed after a [[Skirmish aboard the Albedo Brave|skirmish]] aboard Tapal's flagship, the ''[[Albedo Brave]]'', which ended with the warship's destruction and the escape of a mortally-wounded Tapal and his Padawan [[Cal Kestis]] in an [[escape pod]] to [[Bracca]], although Tapal died from his injuries.<ref name="Jedi: Fallen Order" />

In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of {{Film|III}} to [[19 BBY]].</ref> Mundi and [[Clone Commander]] [[Bacara]] and the Galactic Marines fought on a bridge in a [[Unidentified Mygeeto city|Mygeeto city]] against [[Octuptarra tri-droid]]s, when [[Order 66]] was issued and the clones began to fire at Mundi, killing him.<ref name="ROTS" /> Bacara and the Nova [[Corps]] continued fighting to take out Mygeeto's final [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] positions.<ref name="Helmet Collection 15" /> The Clone Wars formally ended less than a day after Order 66 was issued when Chancellor Palpatine, truly the [[Dark Lord of the Sith]] [[Darth]] Sidious, sent his new [[Sith apprentice|apprentice]], [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], to [[Mustafar]] to [[Mission to Mustafar|kill]] the [[Executive Separatist Council|Separatist Council]] and shut down the Separatist Droid Army. At the same time, Palpatine formally [[Proclamation of the New Order|proclaimed]] the transformation of the Republic into the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="ROTS" />

